          guard echoed a <script> redirect and carried on rendering, so an
          unauthorised user still received the whole page -- 125 KB including the
          patient's results and three editable forms -- and was merely navigated
          away by the browser. curl, view-source or disabled JS kept all of it.

       2. Sentinel-site rule. Only these centres perform lab work, so a facility
          user from anywhere else has no business on this screen even for their own
          patient. National roles are exempt: RCDC enters results for every site. */
    bdsis_require_module();
    if($sid === ''){ bdsis_deny('No laboratory record was specified.'); }
    bdsis_require_subject($bdsis, $sid);
    /* Opening the record needs 'view'. Whether each individual form may be SAVED
